        351.40435791015625,
        542.1077270507812,
        360.3109130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We simulate the model with Milstein’s method and generate data at t ∈[0, 3] with 256 dicretisation steps. The discretisation",
      "bbox": [
        54.97300720214844,
        396.38800048828125,
        541.4415893554688,
        413.673095703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "results in an SSM Zj+1 = f(Zj, ϵj), where Zj ∈R2 encodes C(tj) and R(tj), and ϵj ∈R2 stands for Brownian motion",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        405.6943664550781,
        541.4422607421875,
        427.1230773925781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "increment. We train a neural network to approximate the SDE dynamics by minimising the negative log-likelihood, estimated",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        421.2643737792969,
        541.4411010742188,
        430.1709289550781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by a particle filter with resampling. The neural network is simply a three-layers fully connected network with residual",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        433.2203674316406,
        541.4418334960938,
        442.1269226074219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "connection, see Figure 7, mimicking a discrete SDE solver. No prior knowledge of the dynamics is incorporated into the",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        445.17535400390625,
        541.44140625,
        454.0819091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "neural network. We train the neural network at a fixed 1,000 iterations by the Adam optimiser with learning rate 0.005. At",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        457.13037109375,
        541.4390869140625,
        466.03692626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "testing, we make 100 independent predictions from the learnt model and compute the root mean square error (RMSE) with",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        469.0853576660156,
        541.4420776367188,
        477.9919128417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "respect to a reference trajectory generated using the true dynamics. We use 64 particles, and repeat the experiments 20 times.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        481.0403747558594,
        543.1887817382812,
        489.9469299316406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Results are shown in Tables 11 and 12. Since learning this model is challenging, most methods have experienced divergent",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        498.9733581542969,
        541.44189453125,
        507.8799133300781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "runs. Notably, the diffusion resampling exhibits significantly less divergence, nearly a factor of two lower than the other",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        510.9283447265625,
        541.6052856445312,
        519.8348999023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "methods. Moreover, the prediction error with diffusion resampling is substantially superior than the other methods;",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        522.8833618164062,
        542.2650756835938,
        531.7899169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximately two to five times better. This table is also consistent with that of the LGSSM experiment that the exponential",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        534.83837890625,
        541.4446411132812,
        543.7449340820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "integrators may not propagate SDE gradients effectively, except for Tweedie.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
        546.7943725585938,
        362.03997802734375,
        555.700927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "K. Vision-based pendulum dynamics tracking",
      "bbox": [
        55.44100570678711,
